The core subsystems comprising the zero-trust hardware enclave (`opure-oztae`)
and the binary lifter trampoline engine (`opure-lifter`) are available under
the MIT License for non-commercial, academic, research, and open-source software
distribution.

Proprietary commercial deployments, enterprise SaaS hosting of lifted legacy
binaries, or closed-source commercial operating system distributions utilizing
the OPURE Zero-Trust Agent Enclave (OZTAE) or In-Memory PE32+ Lifter must obtain
an explicit commercial license agreement.

